## The full route map

Memorize these — don't invent new ones.

### Marketing (no auth required)
- `/` — HomePage
- `/employers` — EmployerPage (b2b pitch)
- `/employees` — EmployeePage (b2c pitch; **plural!**)
- `/about`, `/security`, `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/partners`, `/investors`, `/contact`, `/press`

### Auth + onboarding
- `/login` — Login
- `/onboarding` — Onboarding (employee invite-accept entry; **NOT `/signup`**)
- `/employer/onboarding` — OnboardingWizard (employer-side, multi-step)
- `/get-started` → redirects to `/contact`

### Employee portal (role: `employee`)
- `/employee` — EmployeeDashboard
- `/employee/apply` — LoanWizard
- `/employee/loans` — MyLoans
- `/employee/dashboard` → redirects to `/employee`

### Employer portal (role: `employer_admin`)
- `/employer` — EmployerDashboard
- `/employer/employees` — EmployeeRoster (**not** `EmployeesTab.tsx`)
- `/employer/deductions` — DeductionReports
- `/employer/payroll` — PayrollUpload
- `/employer/analytics` — AnalyticsPage
- `/employer/dashboard` → redirects to `/employer`
- `/employer/loans` → redirects to `/employer/deductions`

### Ops / admin portal (roles: `ops`, `admin`, `super_admin`)
- `/ops` — AdminDashboard
- `/ops/review-queue` — ReviewQueue
- `/ops/review-queue/:id` — ReviewDetail
- `/ops/portfolio`, `/ops/employers`, `/ops/alerts`, `/ops/health`
- `/admin` or `/admin/*` → redirect to `/ops`

## Known patterns to respect (not bugs — don't "clean up")

- **`Onboarding.tsx` AND `OnboardingWizard.tsx`** both exist and are both routed. Different purposes: `Onboarding.tsx` is the employee invite-accept flow at `/onboarding`; `OnboardingWizard.tsx` is the employer-side multi-step setup at `/employer/onboarding`. Keep both.
- **`useAuth` custom-claims resolution is complex** — it tries cached token → force-refreshed token → Firestore `employers/{uid}` → Firestore `users/{uid}` with retry. Don't simplify this; it's load-bearing for the different portal entry points.
- **Two CSS files**: `src/styles/index.css` (Tailwind v4 `@theme` + supplemental) and `src/styles/legacy.css` (core component styles). Consolidation is done — don't add a third.

## Shared infrastructure already in place (use, don't re-invent)

- **`@/lib/safeStorage`** — `safeGetItem`, `safeSetItem`, `safeRemoveItem` with try/catch guards. **Always use these** instead of raw `localStorage.*`. Safari private mode / Firefox resist-fingerprinting will throw on raw calls. Shipped in PR #343.
- **Per-portal `<ErrorBoundary>`** in `App.tsx` — each layout (marketing, employee, employer, admin) and each standalone route (`/login`, `/onboarding`, `/*`) is wrapped in its own `ErrorBoundary`. A crash in one page degrades that route only. Don't remove the wrapping.
- **Global `:focus-visible` baseline** — `src/styles/index.css` has a global block that applies teal-900 focus rings to all interactive elements. `.auth-input` is excluded (has its own border-bottom focus style). Don't duplicate focus-visible styles per component.
- **`useRevealOnScroll`** respects `prefers-reduced-motion` — elements get `.vis` immediately if the OS setting is enabled, skipping the intersection-triggered animation. Don't add parallel scroll-animation logic.

## What NOT to do from a frontend task

- Don't modify `functions/`, `services/`, `firestore.rules`, `storage.rules`, `firebase.json`
- Don't install a test runner, form library, or CSS framework as a side quest
- Don't move files to "clean up" the duplicates above without a ticket — they're known
- Don't assume tests exist — if you write `.test.tsx`, you have to wire a runner first (open a ticket)
- Don't commit secrets. `.env.local` is gitignored for dev values
- Don't use raw `localStorage.*` — use `@/lib/safeStorage` helpers
- Don't add a third CSS file — extend `styles/index.css` or `styles/legacy.css`

